            <th scope="col">Gemini API, paid tier</th>
            <th scope="col">Gemini Omni 1.2 Flash</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Input / MTok (text, image, video)</td><td>$1.50</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Text output / MTok</td><td>$9.00</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Video output / MTok</td><td>$12.00</td></tr>
          <tr><td>360p video, per second</td><td>$0.023</td></tr>
          <tr><td>720p video, per second</td><td>About $0.07</td></tr>
          <tr><td>1080p video (upscaled), per second</td><td>$0.104</td></tr>
          <tr><td>4K video (upscaled), per second</td><td>$0.209</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>At 720p a 10-second clip is about $0.70 and a 15-second clip about $1.04 [4]. Google describes the drop as 30%. Its video output price goes from $17.50 per million tokens on Omni 1.1 to $12.00 on 1.2 [4]. The Cloud per-token price is not in the sources on this page.</p>
    <p>The old id <code>gemini-omni-1.1-flash</code> stays available for a four-week transition. From 3 December 2026, requests to it go to <code>gemini-omni-1.2-flash</code> at 1.2 rates [3][4]. That change is inside the Omni line only.</p>
